WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.967
DONALD TRUMP: The United
States will withdraw

00:00:02.967 --> 00:00:06.367
from the Paris Climate Accord.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:10.967
I was elected to represent
the citizens of Pittsburgh,

00:00:10.967 --> 00:00:13.667
not Paris.

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.000
Pittsburgh?

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.066
Now what was upsetting about
that, and that alliteration,

00:00:18.066 --> 00:00:20.567
was the stereotype of our past.

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:23.033
But Pittsburgh is
poised and ready to lead

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:25.000
in the 21st century.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.133
WOMAN 1: We're seeing cities,
and states, and companies,

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.800
and individuals saying,
we are still in,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.734
even with the president pulling
us out of one of the most

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:36.867
important treaties when
every other major country

00:00:36.867 --> 00:00:39.867
in the world has said, we are
gonna come together and commit

00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:42.600
to dealing with climate change.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.400
CHRIS CASTRO: I
continue to be shocked

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.633
at how close the water has being
encroaching just on the beach.

00:00:47.633 --> 00:00:51.900
Sea level rise is completely
apparent in Miami.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.500
FRANK VANCE: We
had six and a half

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.567
foot of water on the main level
of the house for over a week.

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:58.433
Stuff that was in
our bedroom wound up

00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:01.200
in the garage, and stuff
that was in the garage--

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.767
I imagine that's way
down in Louisiana now.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:05.333
ARTURO MASSOL DEYA:
The storms are becoming

00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:07.533
stronger in Puerto Rico.

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:12.900
The worst thing is to think
that that reality will repeat.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.834
STACY HYATT: Not a lot survived
that fire in Ventura County.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:19.533
It burned so hot that
everything just liquefied.

00:01:19.533 --> 00:01:21.667
To not be able to
save anything--

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:22.800
it was just really hard.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.600
MICHAEL MANN: If we're
going to avoid breaching

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.200
catastrophic levels
of warming, we

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.867
need to be putting our foot
on the renewable energy

00:01:30.867 --> 00:01:34.333
acceleration pedal.

00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:37.333
The transformation towards
a renewable energy future

00:01:37.333 --> 00:01:39.934
is the greatest
economic opportunity

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:41.233
of the 21st century.

00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:43.133
RHEA SUH: Businesses
have lined up to say,

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:45.567
we're still committing
to the Paris Accord

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.867
because it's good for
their bottom line.

00:01:47.867 --> 00:01:50.133
DAN LUTAT: My daughter, Faith--
she made the decision that wind

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.300
was where she wanted to be.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.700
This is an opportunity
that hasn't

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.667
been available in America
for a long, long time.

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:56.133
DAVID ANDRADE:
The solar industry

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:57.500
is offering that
second-chance opportunity

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:58.800
to individuals like myself.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.433
CARLOS CURBELO: It
doesn't matter if you're

00:02:00.433 --> 00:02:02.333
a Republican,
Democrat, independent--

00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:03.800
you have a role to play here.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.033
BILL PEDUTO: And if we
look at it as an American

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:10.266
Marshall Plan, we can exceed the
goals of the Paris agreement.

00:02:10.266 --> 00:02:13.533
PROTESTER: This
is the start of us

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:18.367
taking control of our future.

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:20.333
WOMAN 2: We have the
right to a future.

00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:23.166
We have the right to
these basic necessities

00:02:23.166 --> 00:02:25.133
that we need to live.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:29.367
We, the people,
need to take action.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:32.500
Our lives are at stake here.

